  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The analysis is restricted to a specific database of 310 varieties and focuses primarily on gender norms within the United States.",
      "what": "This study analyzed a database of 310 plant-based food varieties (fruits, vegetables, and grains) named after people uninvolved in their development, focusing on the 80 varieties named after women. Using online archival methods and content analysis, the research examined how these women are represented and how these living memorials are commercialized.",
      "why": "It extends the study of gendered commemoration from static monuments and street names into the everyday agricultural landscape, demonstrating that while women are slightly better represented in crop names than in traditional statuary, they remain subject to similar patterns of narrative silencing."
    }
